OL,3,GNEWSAFight of 20 years against
OL,4,Aincinerator ends in minutes
OL,5,
OL,6,FCampaigners said their "20-year fight
OL,7,Fwas over in 20 minutes" after plans
OL,8,Fwere scrapped for a waste incinerator
OL,9,Fwhich has cost the taxpayer #147m and
OL,10,Fhas never been used.
OL,12,FDerby City Council and Derbyshire
OL,13,FCounty Council, which jointly own the
OL,14,FSinfin waste treatment centre, said
OL,15,Fgetting rid of the site would "protect
OL,16,Fthe interests of council taxpayers".
OL,18,FSimon Bacon, former chair of a campaign
OL,19,Fgroup against the project, said the
OL,20,Fnear #150m spend was "money that could
OL,21,Fhave been used in all the projects
OL,22,Facross the city and the county".
OL,23,APub: 25-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
